  "idea": "Raycast vs Alfred: which Mac productivity launcher takes the crown",
  "text": "Comparing Alfred's lightweight workflows against Raycast's built-in AI reveals two distinct productivity philosophies. Alfred consumes negligible memory, but writing custom bash scripts slows down task creation. When generating text or refactoring code, Alfred demands external API keys and complex wiring. Raycast embeds leading AI models directly into your command bar alongside an instant clipboard history manager. You draft messages and manipulate snippets without opening browsers.",
